text: ['({T}: Add {B}.)', '({T}: Add {G}.)', '({T}: Add {R}.)', '({T}: Add {U}.)', '({T}: Add {W}.)', 'Add {R}{R}{R}{R}{R}.', 'All creatures able to block Elvish Bard do so.', 'All creatures get +X/-X until end of turn.', "All lands become 2/2 creatures until end of turn. They're still lands.", 'As Booby Trap enters the battlefield, choose an opponent and a card name other than a basic land card name.\\nThe chosen player reveals each card they draw.\\nWhen the chosen player draws a card with the chosen name, sacrifice Booby Trap. If you do, Booby Trap deals 10 damage to that player.', 'As Story Circle enters the battlefield, choose a color.\\n{W}: The next time a source of your choice of the chosen color would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', 'As long as Storage Matrix is untapped, each player chooses artifact, creature, or land during their untap step. That player can untap only permanents of the chosen type this step.', 'As long as Thran Golem is enchanted, it gets +2/+2 and has flying, first strike, and trample.', "At the beginning of each player's draw step, if Howling Mine is untapped, that player draws an additional card.", "At the beginning of each player's draw step, that player puts the cards in their hand on the bottom of their library in any order, then draws that many cards.", 'At the beginning of each upkeep, create a 1/1 green Saproling creature token.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, Form of the Dragon deals 5 damage to any target.\\nAt the beginning of each end step, your life total becomes 5.\\nCreatures without flying can't attack you.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, if you have 200 or more cards in your library, you win the game.', "At the beginning of your upkeep, if you have a card in hand, return Imaginary Pet to its owner's hand.", 'At the beginning of your upkeep, you draw a card and you lose 1 life.', "Beast of Burden's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creatures on the battlefield.", 'Blaze deals X damage to any target.', 'Change the text of target permanent by replacing all instances of one color word with another or one basic land type with another. (For example, you may change "nonblack creature" to "nongreen creature" or "forestwalk" to "islandwalk." This effect lasts indefinitely.)', 'Choose a color. Target player reveals their hand and discards all cards of that color.', 'Counter target creature spell.', 'Counter target spell unless its controller pays {3}.', 'Counter target spell. Untap up to four lands.', "Creatures and lands target opponent controls don't untap during their next untap step.", "Creatures with power 3 or greater don't untap during their controllers' untap steps.", 'Creatures you control get +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Creatures you control get +1/+1.', 'Creatures you control have flying.', "Creatures you control have vigilance. (Attacking doesn't cause them to tap.)", 'Destroy all Islands.', 'Destroy all Plains.', "Destroy all creatures you don't control. They can't be regenerated.", "Destroy all creatures. They can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy all enchantments.', 'Destroy target artifact or enchantment.', 'Destroy target artifact or land.', 'Destroy target artifact, enchantment, or land.', 'Destroy target artifact.', 'Destroy target attacking creature. You gain life equal to its power.', "Destroy target creature. It can't be regenerated. Its controller reveals cards from the top of their library until they reveal a creature card. The player puts that card onto the battlefield, then shuffles all other cards revealed this way into their library.", 'Destroy target enchantment.', "Destroy target green creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nDraw a card.", 'Destroy target land.', "Destroy target nonblack creature. It can't be regenerated.", 'Destroy target tapped creature.', "Destroy target white creature. It can't be regenerated.\\nDraw a card.", 'Draw four cards.', 'Draw three cards, then discard a card.', 'Draw two cards.', "Dream Prowler can't be blocked as long as it's attacking alone.", 'Each creature gets +1/+1 for each other creature on the battlefield that shares at least one creature type with it. (For example, if two Goblin Warriors and a Goblin Shaman are on the battlefield, each gets +2/+2.)', 'Each player may search their library for up to X creature cards, reveal those cards, put them into their hand, then shuffle.', 'Each player sacrifices four lands. Wildfire deals 4 damage to each creature.', "Each player's life total becomes the number of creatures they control.", "Each spell costs {3} more to cast except during its controller's turn.", "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature doesn't untap during its controller's untap step.", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature gets +0/+2 and has reach. (It can block creatures with flying.)', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 and can't be blocked except by creatures with flying.", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature gets -2/-2.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has fear. (It can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has first strike. (It deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nEnchanted creature has islandwalk. (It can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nWhenever enchanted creature attacks or blocks, its controller loses 3 life.', 'Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\nWhenever enchanted creature deals damage, you gain that much life.', "Enchant creature (Target a creature as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that creature.)\\n{G}: Regenerate enchanted creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature can't attack or block.", 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+1 for each Forest you control.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +1/+2.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature gets +2/+1.', 'Enchant creature\\nEnchanted creature has flying.', 'Enchant creature\\n{R}: Enchanted creature gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', 'Enchant land (Target a land as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that land.)\\nEnchanted land is an Island.', 'Enchant land (Target a land as you cast this. This card enters the battlefield attached to that land.)\\nYou control enchanted land.', 'Enchant land\\nWhenever enchanted land is tapped for mana, its controller adds an additional {G}{G}.', 'Enchant permanent\\nYou control enchanted permanent.', 'Equipped creature gets +2/+2.\\nEquip {2} ({2}: Attach to target creature you control. Equip only as a sorcery.)', 'Equipped creature gets +3/+0 and has trample and lifelink.\\nEquip {3}', "Fear (This creature can't be blocked except by artifact creatures and/or black creatures.)", 'First strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\n{R}: Sandstone Warrior gets +1/+0 until end of turn.', "First strike, protection from black and from red (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike. It can't be blocked, targeted, dealt damage, or enchanted by anything black or red.)", "First strike\\nWhen Nekrataal enters the battlefield, destroy target nonartifact, nonblack creature. That creature can't be regenerated.", "Flame Wave deals 4 damage to target player or planeswalker and each creature that player or that planeswalker's controller controls.", 'Flash', 'Flying', "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nFirst strike (This creature deals combat damage before creatures without first strike.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, you may sacrifice an artifact. If you don't, tap Yawgmoth Demon and it deals 2 damage to you.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nNightmare's power and toughness are each equal to the number of Swamps you control.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nSacrifice Shard Phoenix: It deals 2 damage to each creature without flying.\\n{R}{R}{R}: Return Shard Phoenix from your graveyard to your hand. Activate only during your upkeep.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aven Cloudchaser enters the battlefield, destroy target enchantment.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Aven Fisher dies, you may draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Rathi Dragon enters the battlefield, sacrifice it unless you sacrifice two Mountains.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhen Sage Aven enters the battlefield, look at the top four cards of your library, then put them back in any order.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Blinding Angel deals combat damage to a player, that player skips their next combat phase.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever Thieving Magpie deals damage to an opponent, draw a card.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\nWhenever a creature dealt damage by Sengir Vampire this turn dies, put a +1/+1 counter on Sengir Vampire.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{1}{U}: Return Fleeting Image to its owner's hand.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{1}{U}: Target player reveals the top card of their library.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{B}: Regenerate Will-o'-the-Wisp. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{R}: Shivan Dragon gets +1/+0 until end of turn.", "Flying (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)\\n{W}: Aven Flock gets +0/+1 until end of turn.", 'Flying, vigilance', "Flying, vigilance (This creature can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach, and attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Flying\\nWhen Angel of Mercy enters the battlefield, you gain 3 life.', 'Flying\\nWhen Foul Imp enters the battlefield, you lose 2 life.', 'Flying\\nWhenever Hypnotic Specter deals damage to an opponent, that player discards a card at random.', "Forestwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Goblin Brigand attacks each combat if able.', "Goblin Raider can't block.", 'Guerrilla Tactics deals 2 damage to any target.\\nWhen a spell or ability an opponent controls causes you to discard Guerrilla Tactics, Guerrilla Tactics deals 4 damage to any target.', 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)', "Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nAt the beginning of the end step, return Viashino Sandstalker to its owner's hand. (Return it only if it's on the battlefield.)", "Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nMagnivore's power and toughness are each equal to the number of sorcery cards in all graveyards.", 'Haste (This creature can attack and {T} as soon as it comes under your control.)\\nWhen Thundermare enters the battlefield, tap all other creatures.', 'If a source would deal damage to a permanent or player, it deals double that damage to that permanent or player instead.', 'If an opponent controls more lands than you, search your library for up to three Plains cards, reveal them, put them into your hand, then shuffle.', 'If you control a creature, damage that would reduce your life total to less than 1 reduces it to 1 instead.', "Islandwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls an Island.)", 'Kird Ape gets +1/+2 as long as you control a Forest.', 'Lava Axe deals 5 damage to target player or planeswalker.', 'Look at the top five cards of your library, then put them back in any order.', 'Look at the top two cards of your library. Put one of them into your hand and the other on the bottom of your library.', "Maro's power and toughness are each equal to the number of cards in your hand.", "Mortivore's power and toughness are each equal to the number of creature cards in all graveyards.\\n{B}: Regenerate Mortivore.", "Mountainwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Mountain.)", 'Needle Storm deals 4 damage to each creature with flying.', 'Nonbasic lands are Mountains.', "Ogre Taskmaster can't block.", "Other Elf creatures get +1/+1 and have forestwalk. (They can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Forest.)", 'Other Goblins get +1/+1 and have mountainwalk.', 'Other Zombie creatures get +1/+1.\\n{1}{B}, {T}: Return target Zombie card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'Other creatures you control get +0/+1.', "Phantom Warrior can't be blocked.", "Players play with their hands revealed.\\nIf a player would draw a card, they reveal it instead. Then any other player may pay 2 life. If a player does, put that card into its owner's graveyard. Otherwise, that player draws a card.", 'Prevent all combat damage that would be dealt this turn.', 'Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', 'Put target card from your graveyard on top of your library.', "Put target creature on top of its owner's library.", 'Pyroclasm deals 2 damage to each creature.', 'Reach (This creature can block creatures with flying.)', 'Reach\\n{X}{G}{G}: Silklash Spider deals X damage to each creature with flying.', "Return all creatures to their owners' hands.", 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield.', 'Return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', "Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", 'Sacrifice Bottle Gnomes: You gain 3 life.', 'Sacrifice Sanctum Guardian: The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to any target this turn, prevent that damage.', "Sacrifice a Swamp: Regenerate target black creature. (The next time that creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", "Sacrifice a creature: Draw cards equal to the sacrificed creature's power, then discard three cards.", 'Sacrifice a creature: Nantuko Husk gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', "Sea Monster can't attack unless defending player controls an Island.", 'Search your library for a basic land card, put that card onto the battlefield tapped, then shuffle.', 'Search your library for a card, put that card into your hand, then shuffle.', 'Shock deals 2 damage to any target.', 'Spend only black mana on X.\\nConsume Spirit deals X damage to any target and you gain X life.', "Spineless Thug can't block.", "Sudden Impact deals damage to target player equal to the number of cards in that player's hand.", "Swampwalk (This creature can't be blocked as long as defending player controls a Swamp.)", "Swarm of Rats's power is equal to the number of Rats you control.", 'Tap an untapped creature you control: Llanowar Behemoth gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', 'Target blocking creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', "Target creature gets +3/+3 and gains flying until end of turn. (It can't be blocked except by creatures with flying or reach.)", 'Target creature gets +3/+3 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +7/+7 until end of turn.', 'Target creature gets +X/+0 until end of turn.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You choose a card from it. That player discards that card.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You draw a card for each Forest and green card in it.', 'Target opponent reveals their hand. You draw a card for each Mountain and red card in it.', 'Target opponent sacrifices a creature.', 'Target player discards two cards.', 'Target player gains 8 life.', 'Target player gains X life.', 'Target player loses 4 life and you gain 4 life.', 'Target player loses life equal to the damage already dealt to that player this turn.', 'Target player mills half their library, rounded down.', 'Target player reveals three cards from their hand and you choose one of them. That player discards that card.', 'Target player shuffles their graveyard into their library.', 'Target player untaps all basic lands they control.', 'The next time a source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage. You gain life equal to the damage prevented this way.', "Tidal Kraken can't be blocked.", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)", "Trample (This creature can deal excess combat damage to the player or planeswalker it's attacking.)\\nAt the beginning of your upkeep, Force of Nature deals 8 damage to you unless you pay {G}{G}{G}{G}.", 'Untap all creatures that attacked this turn. After this main phase, there is an additional combat phase followed by an additional main phase.', "Untap all permanents you control during each other player's untap step.", 'Untap target creature and gain control of it until end of turn. That creature gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack and {T} this turn.)', 'Untap target creature. It gets +2/+4 until end of turn.', 'Until end of turn, if target player would draw a card, instead that player skips that draw and you draw a card.', "Up to three target creatures can't block this turn.", "Vigilance (Attacking doesn't cause this creature to tap.)", 'Volcanic Hammer deals 3 damage to any target.', 'When Anarchist enters the battlefield, you may return target sorcery card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Festering Goblin dies, target creature gets -1/-1 until end of turn.', 'When Gravedigger enters the battlefield, you may return target creature card from your graveyard to your hand.', 'When Highway Robber enters the battlefield, target opponent loses 2 life and you gain 2 life.', 'When Hunted Wumpus enters the battlefield, each other player may put a creature card from their hand onto the battlefield.', 'When Kavu Climber enters the battlefield, draw a card.', 'When Mindslicer dies, each player discards their hand.', 'When Phyrexian Gargantua enters the battlefield, you draw two cards and you lose 2 life.', 'When Ravenous Rats enters the battlefield, target opponent discards a card.', 'When Rukh Egg dies, create a 4/4 red Bird creature token with flying at the beginning of the next end step.', 'When Serpent Warrior enters the battlefield, you lose 3 life.', 'When Venerable Monk enters the battlefield, you gain 2 life.', 'When Viridian Shaman enters the battlefield, destroy target artifact.', "When Wanderguard Sentry enters the battlefield, look at target opponent's hand.", 'When Wood Elves enters the battlefield, search your library for a Forest card, put that card onto the battlefield, then shuffle.', 'When you control no other creatures, sacrifice Emperor Crocodile.', 'Whenever Deathgazer blocks or becomes blocked by a nonblack creature, destroy that creature at end of combat.', 'Whenever Elvish Berserker becomes blocked, it gets +1/+1 until end of turn for each creature blocking it.', 'Whenever Hollow Dogs attacks, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Rogue Kavu attacks alone, it gets +2/+0 until end of turn.', 'Whenever Seasoned Marshal attacks, you may tap target creature.', "Whenever a creature becomes the target of a spell or ability, return that creature to its owner's hand. (It won't be affected by the spell or ability.)", "Whenever a creature is dealt damage, destroy it. It can't be regenerated.", 'Whenever a creature you control dies, each other player sacrifices a creature.', 'Whenever a player casts a black spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a blue spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a green spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a red spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a player casts a white spell, you may gain 1 life.', 'Whenever a spell or ability an opponent controls causes a land to be put into your graveyard from the battlefield, return that card to the battlefield.', 'Whenever an opponent casts a spell, Mogg Sentry gets +2/+2 until end of turn.', 'Whenever an opponent discards a card, Megrim deals 2 damage to that player.', 'Whenever an opponent draws a card, Underworld Dreams deals 1 damage to that player.', 'Whenever another creature enters the battlefield, you gain 1 life.', 'Whenever you cast an enchantment spell, you may draw a card.', 'Yavimaya Enchantress gets +1/+1 for each enchantment on the battlefield.', "You and target opponent each flip a coin. Mana Clash deals 1 damage to each player whose coin comes up tails. Repeat this process until both players' coins come up heads on the same flip.", 'You gain 4 life.', 'You have no maximum hand size.', "You have shroud. (You can't be the target of spells or abilities.)", 'You may have Clone enter the battlefield as a copy of any creature on the battlefield.', 'You may play up to three additional lands this turn.', 'Your opponents play with their hands revealed.', "{0}: Return Blinking Spirit to its owner's hand.", '{1}, {T}: Tap target artifact, creature, or land.', '{1}, {T}: You gain 1 life.', "{1}: Return target land you control to its owner's hand.\\n{1}, Discard a land card: Draw a card.", '{1}: The next time a black source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}: The next time a red source of your choice would deal damage to you this turn, prevent that damage.', '{1}{G}: Return target basic land card from your graveyard to your hand.', '{1}{G}: Rootwalla gets +2/+2 until end of turn. Activate only once each turn.', '{1}{W}: The next 1 damage that would be dealt to Zealous Inquisitor this turn is dealt to target creature instead.', "{2}, {T}, Sacrifice Jester's Cap: Search target player's library for three cards and exile them. Then that player shuffles.", '{2}, {T}: Target player mills two cards.', '{2}: Jade Statue becomes a 3/6 Golem artifact creature until end of combat. Activate only during combat.', '{2}{U}{U}: Draw a card.', '{3}, {T}: Rod of Ruin deals 1 damage to any target.', '{3}, {T}: Target player discards a card. Activate only during your turn.', '{4}, {T}, Discard your hand: Draw a card for each creature you control.', "{8}, {T}: Aladdin's Ring deals 4 damage to any target.", '{B}: Looming Shade gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{B}: Regenerate Drudge Skeletons. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{G}, {T}: You may put a creature card from your hand onto the battlefield.', "{G}: Regenerate Ancient Silverback. (The next time this creature would be destroyed this turn, it isn't. Instead tap it, remove all damage from it, and remove it from combat.)", '{R}, Sacrifice Bloodfire Colossus: It deals 6 damage to each creature and each player.', '{R}, {T}: Anaba Shaman deals 1 damage to any target.', '{R}: Flowstone Crusher gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', '{R}: Flowstone Shambler gets +1/-1 until end of turn.', '{R}: Goblin Balloon Brigade gains flying until end of turn.', '{R}: Target creature gains haste until end of turn. (It can attack this turn.)', '{T}, Sacrifice Daring Apprentice: Counter target spell.', '{T}, Sacrifice a creature: Return target creature card from your graveyard to the battlefield. Activate only during your upkeep.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color that a land an opponent controls could produce.', '{T}: Add one mana of any color.', "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Power-Plant, add {C}{C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Mine and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", "{T}: Add {C}. If you control an Urza's Power-Plant and an Urza's Tower, add {C}{C} instead.", '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}, Sacrifice Quicksand: Target attacking creature without flying gets -1/-2 until end of turn.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {G}. Llanowar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {B} or {R}. Sulfurous Springs deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {U}. Yavimaya Coast deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {G} or {W}. Brushland deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {G}. Karplusan Forest deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {R} or {W}. Battlefield Forge deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {B}. Underground River deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {U} or {R}. Shivan Reef deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {B}. Caves of Koilos deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}.\\n{T}: Add {W} or {U}. Adarkar Wastes deals 1 damage to you.', '{T}: Add {C}{C}.', '{T}: Add {G}.', "{T}: All damage that would be dealt to target creature this turn by a source of your choice is dealt to Oracle's Attendants instead.", '{T}: Crossbow Infantry deals 1 damage to target attacking or blocking creature.', '{T}: Destroy target tapped creature.', '{T}: Draw a card, then discard a card.', '{T}: Draw a card.', '{T}: Karplusan Yeti deals damage equal to its power to target creature. That creature deals damage equal to its power to Karplusan Yeti.', '{T}: Orcish Artillery deals 2 damage to any target and 3 damage to you.', '{T}: Prevent the next 1 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Prevent the next 4 damage that would be dealt to any target this turn.', '{T}: Target attacking creature gets +1/+1 until end of turn.', "{T}: Target creature with power 2 or less can't be blocked this turn.", '{T}: Untap target land.', '{U}, {T}: You may tap or untap target creature.', "{U}{U}{U}, {T}: Return target permanent to its owner's hand.", '{W}, Discard a card: You gain 3 life.', '{W}, {T}: Search your library for a land card, reveal it, put it into your hand, then shuffle. Activate only if an opponent controls more lands than you.', '{W}, {T}: Tap target creature.', '{W}: Honor Guard gets +0/+1 until end of turn.', '{X}{W}, {T}: Ballista Squad deals X damage to target attacking or blocking creature.']
flavor: ['"A flash of the lightning, a break of the wave,\\nHe passes from life to his rest in the grave."\\n—William Knox, "Mortality"', '"A good lamp will light your way. A good ring will clear it."\\n—Nervan, royal jeweler', '"Any fool who would die for honor is better off dead."\\n—Cabal Patriarch', '"Are you thinking what I\'m thinking?"', '"Before my eyes was a horrible monster, worthy to figure in the legends of the marvellous. . . . Its eight arms, or rather feet, fixed to its head . . . were twice as long as its body, and were twisted like the furies\' hair."\\n—Jules Verne, *Twenty Thousand Leagues under the Sea*, trans. Lewis', '"Believe in the ideal, not the idol."\\n—Serra', '"Beware lest you lose the substance by grasping at the shadow."\\n—Aesop, *Fables*, trans. Jacobs', '"But high she shoots through air and light,\\nAbove all low delay,\\nWhere nothing earthly bounds her flight,\\nNor shadow dims her way."\\n—Thomas Moore, "Oh that I had Wings"', '"Catch!"', '"Cowards die many times before their deaths;\\nThe valiant never taste of death but once."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Julius Caesar*', '"Don\'t fear the darkness. Fear what it hides."\\n—Remin, venerable monk', '"Don\'t look at it! Maybe it\'ll go away!"\\n—Ib Halfheart, goblin tactician', '"Earth\'s increase, foison plenty,\\nBarns and garners never empty:\\nVines with clust\'ring bunches growing;\\nPlants with goodly burden bowing."\\n—William Shakespeare, *The Tempest*', '"Everything the wise woman learned she wrote in a book, and when the pages were black with ink, she took white ink and began again."\\n—Karn, silver golem', '"For what are leaves but countless blades\\nTo fight a countless foe on high."\\n—Elvish hymn', '"From the snowy slopes of Kaelor,\\nTo the canyons of Bandu,\\nWe drink and fight and feast and die\\nAs we were born to do."\\n—Balduvian tavern song', '"Gambling with mages never is."\\n—Remin, venerable monk', '"Getting people to do what you want is merely a matter of telling them what they want to hear."', '"Graceful? Yes. Beautiful? Absolutely. Harmless? Definitely not."\\n—Fyndhorn elder', '"Guess where I\'m gonna plant this!"', '"Ha, banishment? Be merciful, say \'death,\'\\nFor exile hath more terror in his look,\\nMuch more than death."\\n—William Shakespeare, *Romeo and Juliet*', '"He can split a marshfly in two from halfway across the range."\\n—Onean sergeant', '"He spoke with the tongue of Angels; we fought with the strength of lions."\\n—Handel, infantry soldier', '"Her voice is the wilderness, savage and pure."\\n—Kamahl, druid acolyte', '"Hup, two, three, four,\\nDunno how to count no more."', '"I can staunch their blood, mend their flesh, and knit their bones. But I cannot restore their hope."\\n—Tender-Hand, kitsune healer', '"I confer with Death itself. What could you possibly do to injure me?"', '"I have seen life\'s purpose, and now it is my own."\\n—Kamahl, druid acolyte', '"I hear the roaring of a wave whose waters are red and whose mists are black."\\n—Oracle *en*-Vec', '"I wouldn\'t stand in front of that wurm, son. \'Course, I wouldn\'t stand behind it neither. In fact, standing anywhere near that wurm\'s not much of a plan. Running, now *that\'s* a plan!"\\n—Wandering mage', '"If it is weak, either kill it or ignore it. Anything else honors it."\\n—Kaervek', '"If yesterday was two days ago tomorrow, will the day after tomorrow be today or yesterday?"\\n—Temporal Manipulation 101 final exam, Tolarian Academy', '"In the drowsy dark cave of the mind, dreams build their nest with fragments dropped from day\'s caravan."\\n—Rabindranath Tagore', '"It followed me home. Can I keep it?"', '"It has been my honor to improve on the Thran\'s original design. Perhaps history will remember me in some small part for my work."\\n—Urza, in his apprenticeship', '"Know your foes\' strengths as well as their weaknesses."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi machinist', '"Let everything return to its true nature, so that destiny may take its course."', '"Let\'s go over this one more time. . . ."', '"Let\'s see . . . Mercadia, mercenary, merfolk . . . you know, I really need a better filing system."', '"Men and rats both hunger: we for our playthings; they, for us."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"Mercy? Mercy is for the playground, not the battleground."', '"Most people can\'t build decent weapons out of stone or steel. Trust the elves to do it with only mud and vines."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"My brother, it may now be time to ring the bell and put out the call for aid."', '"My enemy\'s hatred is his weakness. My enemy\'s anger is my strength."\\n—Remin, venerable monk', '"My tales of war are the stories most asked for around the fires at night, but they\'re the ones I care least to tell."', '"Nature cares not for the knowledge to be gained from its study. Better to bleed it dry, lest its potential be wasted on lizards and leaves."', '"Neither could I forget what I had read of these pits—that the *sudden* extinction of life formed no part of their most horrible plan."\\n—Edgar Allan Poe, "The Pit and the Pendulum"', '"No mockeries now for them; no prayers nor bells, / Nor any voice of mourning save the choirs,— / The shrill, demented choirs of wailing shells."\\n—Wilfred Owen, "Anthem for Doomed Youth"', '"No person was ever honored for what he received. Honor has been the reward for what he gave."\\n—Calvin Coolidge', '"Of all I that I have lost, I miss my mind the most."', '"Of all the tyrannies on humane kind\\nThe worst is that which persecutes the mind."\\n—John Dryden,\\n"The Hind and the Panther"', '"Once I saw a goblin shouting at a thunderstorm. He lost the argument pretty quickly."\\n—Wandering mage', '"Over the silver mountains,\\nWhere spring the nectar fountains,\\nThere will I kiss\\nThe bowl of bliss;\\nAnd drink my everlasting fill. . . ."\\n—Sir Walter Raleigh, "The Pilgrimage"', '"Pound the steel until it fits. Doesn\'t work? Bash to bits."\\n—Dwarven forging song', '"Rats, rats, rats! Hundreds, thousands, millions of them, and every one a life."\\n—Bram Stoker, *Dracula*', '"Returne from whence ye came. . . ."\\n—Edmund Spenser, *The Faerie Queene*', '"Rise, and I will show you how to run without flagging, fight without raging, and fly without wings."', '"Secrets? What secrets?"', '"Sit down and read. Educate yourself for the coming conflicts."\\n—Mary Harris "Mother" Jones', '"So they want to kill my men? Well two can play at that game."\\n—General Khurzog', '"Soldiers speak of defending the soil, but they care only for their nations. I care nothing for their nations and everything for the soil."', '"Some believe sandstalkers to be illusions; those with scars know better."\\n—*Zhalfirin Guide to the Desert*', '"Some say it\'s better to think before you act. While those people are considering all the options, that\'s usually when I kill them."\\n—Dravus, lava mage', '"The beauty of mental attacks is that your victims never remember them."\\n—Volrath', '"The bonds of loyalty can tie one to the grave."\\n—Crovax, ascendant evincar', '"The day of Spirits; my soul\'s calm retreat / Which none disturb!"\\n—Henry Vaughan, "The Night"', '"The dead make good soldiers. They can\'t disobey orders, never surrender, and don\'t stop fighting when a random body part falls off."\\n—Nevinyrral, *Necromancer\'s Handbook*', '"The first birth celebrates life. The second birth mocks it."\\n—Mystic elder', '"The hour of your redemption is here. . . . Rally to me. . . . rise and strike. Strike at every favorable opportunity. For your homes and hearths, strike!"\\n—General Douglas MacArthur, to the people of the Philippines', '"The paradox of jade statues is that their victims never really expect attack, but they are never completely surprised either."\\n—Kabel, Tolarian archivist', '"The purest ore is produced from the hottest furnace, and the brightest thunder-bolt is elicited from the darkest storm."\\n—Charles Colton', '"The second wind of ascension is Reaver, slaying the unworthy."\\n—*Keld Triumphant*', '"The tiniest ripple tells a story ten fathoms deep."', '"Their eyes will shrivel and blacken before faith\'s true light."', '"There are as many pillows of illusion as flakes in a snow-storm. We wake from one dream into another dream."\\n—Ralph Waldo Emerson, "Illusions"', '"There was a crack of branches, a rustle of leaves, then a tremendous roar. Our party had no chance as death descended from above."\\n—Taseen, elvish bard', '"There was a wall here. Now it is dust. A tower rose here. Now it is fallen. An army fought here. Now it is dead. A spirit was here. It is all that remains."\\n—Snow-Fur, kitsune poet', '"There\'s an assortment to satisfy all your needs: deep, fleeting, dirty, pure, scientific, philosophical, after, and even fore. For a price."', '"They groaned, they stirred, they all uprose,\\nNor spake, nor moved their eyes;\\nIt had been strange, even in a dream,\\nTo have seen those dead men rise."\\n—Samuel Taylor Coleridge,\\n"The Rime of the Ancient Mariner"', '"This scar? From a zombie\'s teeth. This scar? From a barbarian\'s axe. That scar? I don\'t talk about that one."', '"Though the letter was many pages long, I could tell all I needed to know from one look at the messenger\'s face."\\n—Barrin, master wizard', '"Though there is little to be learned from your dust and stones, I shall wring them dry nevertheless."', '"To examine the causes of life, we must first have recourse to death."\\n—Mary Shelley, *Frankenstein*', '"To think that some find sleep a restful state."\\n—Volrath', '"Tonight, madam, it\'s your money *and* your life."', '"Training? Seeing my crops burnt to cinders was all the \'training\' I needed."', '"True power is controlling not only the hearts of your subjects, but their minds as well."', '"We are not interested in the possibilities of defeat."\\n—Queen Victoria', '"Wealth means power; the power to subdue, to crush, to exploit, the power to enslave, to outrage, to degrade."\\n—Emma Goldman, "Anarchism"', '"Well, it also makes a very nice flower pot. . . ."\\n—Arcum Dagsson, Soldevi machinist', '"What can a peasant get for free that an emperor can never buy?"\\n—Dal riddle', '"What do you have that I cannot obtain?"\\n—Mairsil, the Pretender', '"What\'s better than smashing things with a rock? A rock that gets up and smashes things for you."\\n—Toggo, goblin weaponsmith', '"When the air burns, only death breathes deep."\\n—Bogardan mage', '"Who\'s the crazy one now!?"\\n—Torgle, mountaintop boatmaker', '"Why do we pray to the Ancestor? Because She listens."\\n—Mystic elder', '"Wisdom is not the counting of all the drops in a waterfall. Wisdom is learning why the water seeks the earth."', '"You can run from your pain, but you will tire before it does."\\n—Gerrard of the *Weatherlight*', '"Your blood, your marrow, your spirit—all are mine."\\n—Mayvar, minion of Geth', 'A blade that has never known sheath, a hilt that has never known hand.', 'A bored wizard once created a vizzerdrix out of a bunny and a piranha. He never made *that* mistake again.', 'A drop of humanity for a sea of power.', 'A full coffin is like a full coffer—both are attractive to thieves.', 'A hollow dog is never empty. It is filled with thirst for the hunt.', 'A skilled decoy can throw your enemies off your trail. A master decoy can survive to do it again.', 'A wurm knows nothing of deception. If it opens its mouth, it plans to eat you.', 'After years of training, the druid becomes one with nature, drawing power from the land and returning it when needed.', 'Age wears the flesh but galvanizes the soul.', 'Armodons are trained to step on things. Enemy things.', "As a beaver's teeth grow unchecked without regular use, so does the golem's armor grow without regular battles.", 'As long as the dryads are a part of the forest, the forest is a part of the army.', "Barrin's pride in his apprentice was diminished somewhat when he had to get the others back down.", 'Behind his eyes is the pain of every soldier his hands have healed.', 'Bitter as wormwood, sweet as mulled wine.', 'Bright as a mirror, dark as the sea.', 'Called "stonefeathers" by many lowlanders, rukhs are thought to descend from a phoenix that sacrificed its flame for a body of stone.', 'Count carefully the souls and see that none are lost.\\n—Vec teaching', "Don't try to outrun one of Dominaria's grizzlies; it'll catch you, knock you down, and eat you. Of course, you could run up a tree. In that case you'll get a nice view before it knocks the tree down and eats you.", 'Dry grass is tinder before the spark.', 'Dwell longest on the thoughts that shine brightest.', 'Each victory adds a new verse.', 'Empires rise and fall, but evil is eternal.', 'Even the brave are scared by a lion three times: first by its tracks, again by its roar, and one last time face to face.\\n—Somali proverb', 'Every branch a crossroads, every vine a swift steed.', 'Every litter of kavu yields one cub that refuses to hunt with the pack.', 'Fire finds its form in the heat of the forge.', 'Fire is always at the top of the food chain, and it has a *big* appetite.', 'Fire never dies alone.', 'Flowstone troops are notoriously difficult to keep in formation.', 'Follow the pathmage\\n—Otarian expression meaning "escape quickly"', 'For the first time in his life, Grakk felt a little warm and fuzzy inside.', 'Fortunately, hill giants have large blind spots in which a human can easily hide. Unfortunately, these blind spots are beneath the bottoms of their feet.', "From Gaea grew the world, and the world was silent. From Gaea grew the world's elves, and the world was silent no more.\\n—Elvish teaching", "Goblins' motivational techniques are crude, but effective.", 'Gravity is truly what you make of it.', 'Greed and gluttony led him to death. Now they are his greatest assets.', 'He raged at the world, at his family, at his life. But mostly he just raged.', "He's smart for a goblin. He can do two things: hit *and* run.", 'Healers ultimately acquire the divine gifts of spiritual and physical wholeness. The most devout are also granted the ability to pass physical wholeness on to others.', 'Heavy light flooded across the landscape, cloaking everything in deep crimson.', "Helplessly drawn in, the bard's enemies quickly find there's more than song to be found.", "Her roots connect her to the forest's wishes.", 'His peers derive knowledge from ancient tomes locked within dark spires. He finds knowledge within the solitude of a lifetime spent watching the Quicksilver Sea.', 'If taken, it cuts the hand that clutches it. If given, it heals the hand that holds it.', "If you find yourself and a friend being chased by a king cheetah, you have but one chance: Trip your friend.\\n—Suq'Ata wisdom", "If you try to sneak up on a rootwalla, you'll suddenly find yourself dealing with twice the lizard.", "If you're smaller than the anaconda, it considers you food. If you're larger than the anaconda, it considers you a lot of food.", 'In addition to killing peasants, punishing subordinates, and raising an army of nightmares, Braids somehow found time for her favorite hobby: petty extortion.', 'In fire there is the spark of chaos and destruction, the seed of life. In ice there is perfect tranquility, perfect order, and the silence of death.', 'In front of every great wizard is a doomed apprentice.', 'In life, it was a fetid, disease-ridden thing. In death, not much changed.', 'Infantry deployment is the art of putting your troops in the wrong place at the right time.', 'It *is* the thing that goes bump in the night.', 'It allows those with dangerous weapons to pass. But not those with dangerous thoughts.', "It doesn't like having visitors . . . unless it's having them for lunch.", "It doesn't think. It doesn't feel.\\nIt doesn't laugh or cry.\\nAll it does from dusk till dawn\\nIs make the soldiers die.\\n—Onean children's rhyme", "It entered the temple with all the pomp and decorum of a rock hitting a goblin's skull.", 'It lights up the sky, beckoning enemies only to repel them.', 'It lives mainly on fruit, leaves, and the occasional nose.', 'It may look like soil, but its nature is malice.', 'It puts the "fur" in "fury."', 'It still stares accusingly at Memnarch, though millennia have passed since he separated the eye from its body.', 'It took all its strength to contain the fire within.', "It's easy to believe the monster is a myth—until you feel three hundred thousand pounds of myth crashing down on your ship.", 'Its curve mimics the twists of life and death.', 'Its diet consists of fruits, plants, small woodland animals, large woodland animals, woodlands, fruit groves, fruit farmers, and small cities.', 'Its eye the glaring sun, its cry the keening wind.', 'Its hooves strike lightning and the thunder follows quickly after.', 'Just as each added feather steadies the wing, so does the flock grow stronger with each new member.', 'Just one can feed a dozen people for a month.', 'Just try taking *this* bull by the horns.', 'Keldon soldiers learn to move faster than the whip.', "Krosa's distorted groves bear strange fruit.", 'Leave the door to the past even slightly ajar and it could be blown off its hinges.', 'Legend has it that the mine howls out the last words of those who died inside.', 'Like a loaded cannon—point and shoot.', 'Like the tide, time both ebbs and flows.', 'Little dreamt could seem so cruel\\nAs waiting for the wings outspread,\\nThe jagged teeth, the burning eyes,\\nAnd dagger-claws that clench to nerves.', "Made from its wearer's hopes, the mask ensures that those hopes will be fulfilled.", 'Mold crept over the walls and into every crevice until the gleaming white stone strained and burst.', 'More than one mage has been driven insane by the sound of the millstone relentlessly grinding away.', 'Nature grows solutions to her problems.', 'No one knows whether they were named for the disease they carry or for the speed at which they multiply.', 'No two see the same Maro.', 'Nothing is sacred to the rats. Everything is simply another meal.', 'Nothing makes a mogg madder than having to wake up.', 'Of royal blood among the spirits of the air, the Mahamoti djinn rides on the wings of the winds. As dangerous in the gambling hall as he is in battle, he is a master of trickery and misdirection.', 'On darkness feeding, in nightmares breeding.', "Once he'd worked out which end of the thing was sharp, he was promoted to guard duty.", 'One bone broken for every twig snapped underfoot.\\n—Llanowar penalty for trespassing', 'Only the warrior who can admit mortal weakness will be bolstered by immortal strength.', 'Other Phyrexians have nightmares about the gargantua.', 'Other birds collect twigs for their nests. Magpies steal jewels for theirs.', "Pray that it doesn't seek the safety of your lungs.", 'Reinforcements . . . or refreshments?', 'She stands as a living symbol of the natural world and an enemy of the forces that threaten it.', 'Some fishers like to eat eels, and some eels like to eat fishers.', 'Sometimes everyone decides to go for help at the same time.', 'Sometimes the greatest strength is the strength of conviction.', 'Spirit is the sword and experience the sharpening stone.\\n—Arabian proverb', 'Storm crow descending, winter unending. Storm crow departing, summer is starting.', 'Such power grows the body as it shrinks the soul.', 'Such power protects the body with the strength of the soul.', 'Summer sends its kiss with warmth and blooming life.', 'The College of Lat-Nam is often forced to expel students whose experiments grow too risky or too cruel.', 'The barbarians call it "touching the soul of the dragon."', "The bears had been isolated on an island for hundreds of years, until the island sank and the bears didn't.", 'The best ideas often come from the worst minds.', "The bloom contains no seeds. It's meant only to nourish the forest's inhabitants.", 'The bodies of its victims are the only tracks it leaves.', 'The dying ask for water because they know it contains life.', 'The earth cannot hold that which magic commands.', 'The elves had the edge in guile, skill, and valor. But in the end, only sheer numbers mattered.', 'The fatal flaw in every plan is the assumption that you know more than your enemy.', 'The fruit of this fabled tree takes on the flavor of whatever food you love most.', 'The furnace awaits the next master who would stoke the fires of apocalypse.', 'The goblin word for "flying" is more accurately translated as "falling slowly."', 'The hardest part of his training is learning not to eat the boar.', 'The imp, unaware of its own odor, paused to catch its breath . . . and promptly died.', "The king of Yavimaya's waters pays constant attention to his subjects . . . and thrives on their adulation.", 'The knight knelt and prayed, first for the sanctity of his land and second for the strength to repel its invaders.', 'The most terrifying thing about the craw wurm is probably the horrible crashing sound it makes as it speeds through the forest. This noise is so loud it echoes through the trees and seems to come from all directions at once.', 'The only thing that flies over the Krosan Forest is the wind.', 'The only thing worse than a goblin is a goblin that knows his way around.', 'The pain of a lifetime—every scrape, illness, and bruise—condensed into a single moment.', 'The pattern of life can be studied like a book, if you know how to read it.', 'The perfect antidote for a tightly packed formation.', 'The rain is driven like nails.', 'The rod is a relic from ancient times . . . cruel, vicious, mean-spirited times.', 'The same spears that catch their food today will defend their homes tomorrow.', 'The skyhunters were born when the first leonin gazed at the heavens and wished to hunt the birds overhead.', 'The song of the forest is in perfect harmony. If a single note is out of place, the elves will find its source.', 'The soul sheds light, and death is its shadow. When the light dims, life and death embrace.\\n—Nantuko teaching', 'The strength of one. The courage of ten.', 'The thunder of its hooves beats dreams into despair.', "The turning of the tide always begins with one soldier's decision to head back into the fray.", 'The undisputed master of the mountains of Shiv.', 'The vines and branches of the jungle canopy are all the wings it needs.', 'The wise pay as much attention to what they throw away as to what they keep.', 'The wise, the righteous, the mighty—the merchant feeds them all.', 'The wizard who reads a thousand books is powerful. The wizard who memorizes a thousand books is insane.', 'The wurms become so big, a single scale can be used as a roof for a human dwelling.', 'Their fury scatters enemies like a pile of dry leaves.', 'They are incubated by swamp gases and cut their teeth on zombie flesh. Serpent warriors are not to be trifled with.', 'They follow the prophecy to each new prophet, guarding the future from the present.', 'They patched the holes, loaded their sharpest rocks, spanked their children one last time, and lurched off into the sunset.', 'Think of it as a butcher knife with wings.', 'Those who will not follow are doomed to lead.', "Though it was built as an instrument of labor, it wasn't long before it became an instrument of war.", 'Though no longer attached to the hand, it still holds its adversary in its grasp.', 'Three little goblins, enjoying their brew. One bumped an ogre, and then there were two.', "Tired doesn't even begin to cover it.", 'To be king, Numsgil did in Blog, who did in Unkful, who did in Viddle, who did in Loll, who did in Alrok. . . .', "To merfolk, pirates are a nuisance. To pirates, merfolk are a threat. To the kraken, they're both appetizers.", "Toren had stepped on a lot of bugs during his life, so he couldn't help feeling embarrassed when a bug stepped on him.", 'Trained in the arts of stealth, royal assassins choose their victims carefully, relying on timing and precision rather than brute force.', 'Watching the spider\'s web\\n—Llanowar expression meaning "focusing on the wrong thing"', 'What burns the land, boils the seas.', 'What it lacks in backbone, it makes up for in cruelty.', 'When she flies above the good, they consider themselves blessed. When she flies above the wicked, they consider themselves dead.', 'When your enemies are denied soldiers, they are denied victory.', 'Which is more unsettling: the roar of battle or the silence that follows?', 'Wine and balm for the confessions of the repentant. Razors and irons for the confessions of the unrepentant.', 'You are who you eat.', 'You should see how small the map is.', "You won't know what you're missing.", 'Your entire life passes before its eyes.']
artist: ['Adam Rex', 'Adrian Smith', 'Alan Pollack', 'Alan Rabinowitz', 'Alex Horley-Orlandelli', 'Allen Williams', 'Andrew Goldhawk', 'Andrew Robinson', 'Anson Maddocks', 'Anthony S. Waters', 'Arnie Swekel', 'Ben Thompson', 'Bob Eggleton', 'Bob Petillo', 'Brian Despain', 'Brian Snõddy', 'Brom', 'Carl Critchlow', 'Chippy', 'Christopher Moeller', 'Christopher Rush', 'Corey D. Macourek', 'D. Alexander Gregory', 'D. J. Cleland-Hura', 'Dan Frazier', 'Dana Knutson', 'Daniel Gelon', 'Dany Orizio', 'Daren Bader', 'Darrell Riche', 'Dave Dorman', 'David Martin', 'Dermot Power', 'DiTerlizzi', 'Donato Giancola', 'Doug Chaffee', 'Douglas Shuler', 'Edward P. Beard, Jr.', 'Eric Deschamps', 'Francis Tsai', 'Franz Vohwinkel', 'Fred Fields', 'Gary Leach', 'Gary Ruddell', 'Glen Angus', 'Greg Hildebrandt', 'Greg Hildebrandt & Tim Hildebrandt', 'Greg Staples', 'Heather Hudson', 'Hugh Jamieson', 'Iain McCaig', 'James Bernardin', 'Janine Johnston', 'Jason Alexander Behnke', 'Jeff Miracola', 'Jeremy Jarvis', 'Jim Murray', 'Jim Nelson', 'Jim Pavelec', 'John Avon', 'John Bolton', 'John Howe', 'John Matson', 'Justin Sweet', 'Kev Walker', 'Larry Elmore', 'Lars Grant-West', 'Luca Zontini', 'Mark Romanoski', 'Mark Tedin', 'Mark Zug', 'Martina Pilcerova', 'Matt Cavotta', 'Matt Thompson', 'Matthew D. Wilson', 'Matthew Mitchell', 'Melissa A. Benson', 'Michael Sutfin', 'Mike Dringenberg', 'Mike Kerr', 'Mike Ploog', 'Nick Percival', 'Nicola Leonard', 'Paolo Parente', 'Patrick Ho', 'Pete Venters', 'Puddnhead', 'Ralph Horsley', 'Randy Elliott', 'Randy Gallegos', 'Rebecca Guay', 'Richard Kane Ferguson', 'Richard Sardinha', 'Rick Farrell', 'Rob Alexander', 'Robert Bliss', 'Roger Raupp', 'Ron Spears', 'Ron Spencer', 'Scott Bailey', 'Scott M. Fischer', 'Simon Bisley', 'Stephen Tappin', 'Steve Luke', 'Stuart Griffin', 'Ted Naifeh', 'Terese Nielsen', 'Thomas Gianni', 'Thomas M. Baxa', 'Todd Lockwood', 'Tom Fleming', 'Tom Kyffin', 'Tom Wänerstrand', 'Tony Szczudlo', 'Una Fricker', 'Val Mayerik', 'Vance Kovacs', 'Wayne England', 'rk post']
